 "ez_index": 221,
 "name": "ST37EV_EVENT00.BBQ",
 "strings": [
  "",
  "The war between the AEUG",
  "and the Titans was not fought",
  "only in the Gryps area.",
  "The AEUG already believed",
  "that a full-scale",
  "armed clash with the Titans",
  "was unavoidable, and",
  "it worked everywhere to build up",
  "its fleet strength.",
  "Mobile suits or no,",
  "without ships to carry",
  "and maintain them, it was",
  "all just a local revolt.",
  "A space fleet, formed",
  "to deploy its forces",
  "with speed and flexibility,",
  "was the AEUG's cherished dream.",
  "Ships that, on paper,",
  "had been sunk--",
  "Federation and Zeon vessels;",
  "wrecks salvaged by way",
  "of junk dealers;",
  "ships built from diverted supplies;",
  "and in the end even",
  "the fleets of Zeon remnants:",
  "by every means there was,",
  "they added more ships",
  "to the AEUG.",
  "Even after the Delaz rebellion,",
  "the Earth Federation showed",
  "no interest in space.",
  "Keeping watch over the whole vast",
  "Earth Sphere for signs of unrest",
  "is a tiresome business.",
  "The Federation",
  "loathed such petty chores,",
  "and was content to hand it all",
  "to the Titans, oddballs who",
  "actually asked to go",
  "and stamp out Zeon.",
  "To them,",
  "space was only the frontier,",
  "and if hundreds of thousands",
  "of colony residents died there, it",
  "was news, soon forgotten.",
  "But to the people of space,",
  "it was not so.",
  "As their forefathers had done,",
  "they scrimped on",
  "scarce materials,",
  "doggedly repaired wrecks,",
  "scraped together mobile suits,",
  "and formed fleets.",
  "Some ships even deserted",
  "the Federation Forces without",
  "a thought for what came next.",
  "The AEUG's Finances",
  "Junk Dealers",
  "The AEUG was, at bottom,",
  "a poor household.",
  "Though it had the backing of",
  "donations from lunar and colony",
  "capitalists, its budget could",
  "never match the plenty enjoyed by",
  "the Federation Forces and Titans,",
  "backed as they were by",
  "the Earth Federation itself.",
  "But for that very reason, it took",
  "care over its members' welfare.",
  "First and foremost came a system",
  "that never let pay",
  "arrive late.",
  "This is what led",
  "regular troops tired of late pay,",
  "and veterans laid off and adrift",
  "with nowhere to go, to throw in",
  "their lot with the AEUG.",
  "Next, the AEUG's leaders",
  "took great pains over food.",
  "With no fixed base of its own,",
  "the AEUG had no choice",
  "but to make its ships its home.",
  "So in that closed environment,",
  "good meals were absolutely",
  "essential.",
  "Emma Sheen, who came over",
  "from the Titans, an elite unit,",
  "was astonished by the food",
  "aboard the Argama,",
  "which bears this out.",
  "They were a cheerful army.",
  "It was not that they had",
  "bright prospects ahead,",
  "and one may doubt whether",
  "they could win.",
  "But they risked their lives,",
  "fighting for the families awaiting",
  "their return, and for their homes.",
  "They fully meant",
  "to come home alive,",
  "and spared no effort",
  "to do so.",
  "For that reason,",
  "they worked hard to cut costs,",
  "and prototypes, captured units,",
  "and other normally unused",
  "mobile suits",
  "were sent to the front as well.",
  "That those machines stayed",
  "operational to the very end",
  "was owed to the AEUG members'",
  "superhuman efforts, and the fine",
  "welfare behind them, nothing else.",
  "The destruction the One Year War",
  "wrought is beyond counting, but",
  "the greatest of it all",
  "was space debris,",
  "in other words, garbage in space.",
  "In space,",
  "even a single screw or shard",
  "of armor flies on, keeping",
  "the speed and kinetic energy",
  "it had at the moment",
  "of its destruction.",
  "A mobile suit fragment, say,",
  "moving at supersonic speed",
  "will go on at supersonic speed",
  "forever.",
  "If it strikes a colony or ship,",
  "the damage will be severe,",
  "needless to say.",
  "Even the Federation government,",
  "reluctant to arm any colony,",
  "allowed them, if nothing else,",
  "large laser cannons",
  "for breaking up debris.",
  "These lasers were powerful",
  "enough to destroy",
  "large meteorites.",
  "And the One Year War spawned,",
  "besides the wrecks of older ships,",
  "the bodies of crews, mobile suits,",
  "space battleships, and even",
  "colony fragments--a staggering",
  "mass of debris.",
  "It was feared that debris,",
  "through further mishaps, would",
  "breed more, until at last travel",
  "between space and Earth became",
  "impossible: the so-called",
  "Kessler syndrome, the turning",
  "of space into a desert.",
  "Thus,",
  "after the One Year War, clearing",
  "space junk became a top priority.",
  "Even so,",
  "no one had the means",
  "to do it at public expense, so",
  "little by little,",
  "\"Whatever is found in space,",
  " no matter what it is, belongs",
  " to the one who finds it\"",
  "--that unwritten law",
  "of the spacemen came",
  "to be applied.",
  "Somehow, people had to be",
  "given a reason to pick up",
  "the garbage.",
  "And so",
  "junk dealing became the busiest",
  "trade in the whole Earth Sphere.",
  "Big: a battleship's fusion reactor.",
  "Small: electronic parts.",
  "Even mobile suit fragments,",
  "gathered up and recycled,",
  "made vast fortunes.",
  "Above all, it was seen as work",
  "that protected their own homes,",
  "and that earned them the respect",
  "of the people of space.",
  "They built a society of their own,",
  "with a power that even the",
  "Colony Corporation respected.",
  "Pergamino, who on Side 6,",
  "independent of the Federation,",
  "Zeon, and Side 6 alike,",
  "serviced both armies' ships",
  "and made a vast fortune.",
  "Gemon Bajack, of the Side 1",
  "Bunch 1 colony, who went so far",
  "as to develop his own MS.",
  "Meitzer Ronah, who rose from",
  "junk dealer to become the owner",
  "of a colony.",
  "These are among the best known.",
  "This, of course,",
  "worked in the AEUG's favor too.",
  "They diligently",
  "plied the junk dealer's trade,",
  "and so could build a fleet",
  "that officially did not exist.",
  "And so",
  "the AEUG fleet, now complete,",
  "rose up across space and",
  "struck in force at the Titans",
  "fleet then massing",
  "in Earth orbit.",
  "Space was their home, and",
  "this was their declaration",
  "that the Titans",
  "would not be allowed",
  "to do as they pleased there",
  "forever.",
  "Their victory in this battle",
  "made the AEUG widely known",
  "among the people of space.",
  "Seeing that space emigrants",
  "would not just keep taking",
  "it from the people of Earth,",
  "even those who had thought",
  "the AEUG all talk",
  "began to give money",
  "of their own accord.",
  "Nor was it only capitalists;",
  "from meager savings",
  "and meager wages, they gave",
  "to the AEUG,",
  "billions of the people of space",
  "in one enormous wave."
 ]
}
